---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getProductBrief } from '../../data/ai-products';
const briefs = [getProductBrief("service-desk-toolbox")!,getProductBrief("deep-research")!];
---
<Base description="Service desk workflows and ticket investigations, with an interactive fictional demo." title="Service Toolbox"><p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/projects/">← Projects</a></p><h1>Service Toolbox</h1><p class="intro">A workspace for the service desk. Investigate a sample ticket, inspect the evidence, and review the next steps.</p>{briefs.map(brief => <section class="product-context"><h2>{brief.name}</h2><p class="meta">{brief.role} · {brief.status}</p><p>{brief.tagline}</p><ul>{brief.capabilities.map(capability => <li>{capability}</li>)}</ul><p>{brief.shipped}</p><p class="meta">Production stack: {brief.stack.join(' · ')}</p></section>)}<h2>Design choices</h2><p>The investigation stays attached to a ticket. Evidence and proposed next steps are visible before an action is taken, and writeback remains a human decision. The replica lets you inspect that boundary without connecting to the service desk.</p><h2>Explore a sample</h2><p class="meta">Interactive replica of my work · Fictional data · Selected interactions</p><p><a href="/demos/service-toolbox/">Open full-screen ↗</a></p><iframe class="demo-frame" src="/demos/service-toolbox/" title="Service Toolbox interactive replica" loading="lazy"></iframe><h2>Keeping track of what runs</h2><p>The Status view brings execution history, estimated time returned, and open follow-ups into one report.</p><p><a href="/demos/status/">Open Status full-screen ↗</a></p><iframe class="demo-frame" src="/demos/status/" title="Status interactive replica" loading="lazy"></iframe><p><a href="/years/2026/">The team’s automation process and published case study →</a></p></Base>